Survivors:
- SM8 (equivalent): the cleared storage of an account absent on the other side. A diff is only ever applied
  to the state it was computed from, where that account is absent, so its entry starts empty anyway.
- SM10 (a guard, not reachable): marking unreachable states pruned. In the first pass it survived and showed a
  real gap: a kept side state held only as a diff could become unreachable. Fixed in 4b49d03 (kept side states
  are made full), which SM11 checks. Since then no state can become unreachable, so SM10 is a guard.
